29. How the module creates three servers

Your input:

instances = {

  web1 = {
    subnet_key = "subnet1"
    ...
  }

  web2 = {
    subnet_key = "subnet2"
    ...
  }

  web3 = {
    subnet_key = "subnet3"
    ...
  }
}

produces:

                    Internet
                       │
                       ▼
                ┌────────────┐
                │    ALB     │
                │    :80     │
                └─────┬──────┘
                      │
          ┌───────────┼───────────┐
          │           │           │
          ▼           ▼           ▼
       web1        web2        web3
       EC2         EC2         EC2
       :80         :80         :80
          │           │           │
          ▼           ▼           ▼
      subnet1     subnet2     subnet3
      10.0.1/24   10.0.2/24   10.0.3/24
          │           │           │
          └───────────┼───────────┘
                      ▼
                     VPC
                  10.0.0.0/16

The important Terraform relationship is:

for_each = var.instances

which creates:

aws_instance.web["web1"]
aws_instance.web["web2"]
aws_instance.web["web3"]

Then:

for_each = aws_instance.web

automatically registers those instances with the target group.

