13. Create a Terraform module version

This is a very important practice.

Instead of calling:

?ref=master

use a version:

v1.0.0

Create the tag:

git tag v1.0.0

Push it:

git push origin v1.0.0

Now your local Terraform project can use:

source = "git::https://github.com/gopal1409/terraform-aws-blue-green-module-july10.git//modules/networking?ref=v1.0.0"

This is better because your infrastructure will continue using the same module version even if you later change the master branch.

